      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not uncommon for the operated leg to be more swollen and sensitive immediately after surgery due to pain, bruising, and the body's natural healing process. However, if you experience sharp pain, severe numbness, tingling, or difficulty moving your leg, it's best to consult your surgeon or doctor. They can assess your condition and provide guidance on managing your symptoms and determining the cause of the unusual symptoms you're experiencing. It's always better to err on the side of caution when it comes to surgical recovery.",
